// Regicide - Isafdar navigation obstacles (checklist item #5).
// Locs are still only declared in scripts/_unpack/377/all.loc (unmigrated), same situation
// quest_upass's upass_obstacles.rs2 already relies on for several of its own obstacles.
//
// Dense forest is a hard Agility level gate that cannot be failed - you either meet the level or
// you don't, and Lord Iorwerth's crystal pendant is the alternative to meeting it.
//
// Leaf trap / tripwire / stick trap: all three are obstacles that MOVE YOU when you pass them, and
// all three scale with Agility. The numbers are the wiki's own, from Leaves_(trap), Tripwire and
// Sticks_(trap) - a straight line in Agility level from the level-1 figure to the level-99 one:
//
//   leaves    70.7% at 1 -> 100%   at 99   fail: up to 18 damage, and you climb out YOUR side
//   tripwire  12.11% at 1 -> 60.94% at 99  fail: 10 damage and poison, and you stay put
//   sticks    12.1% at 1 -> 60.9%  at 99   fail: knocked back for 8 damage
//
// They used to be flat one-in-eight / one-in-ten rolls that ignored Agility entirely, and - far
// worse - none of the three moved the player at all. Two of them are the only link between parts
// of Isafdar: the sticks at 2295,3214 are the one gap in the trees between the Well of Voyage's
// clearing and the forest west of it, and the tripwire at 2294,3243 is the one gap going north.
// Flood-filled, the clearing reaches 534 tiles and stops dead, so Regicide could not be played
// past its second step and neither could anything else in Tirannwn.

// ===== Dense forest: regicide_cross_over1/2/3 (Isafdar) + _tyras_camp variants, op1=Enter =====
[oploc1,regicide_cross_over1] @regicide_cross_forest;
[oploc1,regicide_cross_over2] @regicide_cross_forest;
[oploc1,regicide_cross_over3] @regicide_cross_forest;
[oploc1,regicide_cross_over1_tyras_camp] @regicide_cross_forest;
[oploc1,regicide_cross_over2_tyras_camp] @regicide_cross_forest;

[label,regicide_cross_forest]
// checklist item #6: Lord Iorwerth's crystal pendant is an alternate pass condition, not a
// replacement for the 56 Agility route - either one lets the player through.
if(stat(agility) < 56 & inv_total(inv, regicide_crystal_pendant) < 1) {
    ~mesbox("You need an Agility level of 56 to get through this dense forest.");
    return;
}
def_coord $end = ~regicide_obstacle_end(loc_coord, 3, 2, loc_angle);
mes("You push your way through the dense forest...");
p_delay(0);
// ~forcewalk2 CANNOT CROSS THIS, and it is the whole point of the obstacle. forcewalk2 goes
// through ~clipped_telewalk, which checks map_blocked on every single tile of the way and gives up
// silently the moment one of them is solid - and a band of dense forest is solid by definition.
// So the player got "You push your way through the dense forest..." followed by "...and come out
// the other side.", and stood exactly where they had been standing.
//
// That was not a cosmetic failure. Flood-filled on the ground plane, the band the Well of Voyage
// puts you out into is 365 tiles and the band Iorwerth Camp stands in is 1,293, and the two do not
// share a single pair of adjacent tiles: every one of the fifteen crossings in Isafdar is a loc
// sitting in solid scenery with open ground two tiles the other side. Nothing else joins them.
// Regicide stopped dead at the first band for everyone, and so did the half of Mourning's End that
// crosses the same forest.
//
// ~forcemove is the unclipped walk - the same proc West Ardougne's blocked doors use to step a
// player through a wall - and it is what an obstacle that crosses something solid has to use.
~forcemove($end);
mes("...and come out the other side.");

// ===== Where an obstacle puts you =====
// Straight on through, on the axis you walked up to it from, as far as the first tile beyond it
// you can actually stand on.
//
// A fixed distance does not work here and that is worth writing down, because it is why this
// quest could not be walked. The bands of scenery the Isafdar obstacles cross are not all the same
// thickness: the forest band at 2302,3214 is two tiles of solid ground, a leaf pit is three, and
// the three crossings in a row at x=2266/2269/2272 on z=3191 are a nine-tile wall with the two
// middle crossings standing inside it. ~forcemove does not check clipping - which is the only
// reason it can cross any of them - so a fixed two tiles left the player standing in the middle of
// the scenery on most of them, which looks exactly like the obstacle having done nothing.
[proc,regicide_obstacle_end](coord $loc, int $w, int $l, int $angle)(coord)
// The loc's width and length are passed in because the footprint decides which side the player is
// standing on, and loc_coord is only its origin corner. GameMap measures the footprint at the
// loc's original angle and swaps the two on an odd one, so this does the same.
def_int $sx = $w;
def_int $sz = $l;
if ($angle = 1 | $angle = 3) {
    $sx = $l;
    $sz = $w;
}
def_int $dx = 0;
def_int $dz = 0;
if (coordz(coord) > add(coordz($loc), sub($sz, 1))) {
    $dz = -1;
} else if (coordz(coord) < coordz($loc)) {
    $dz = 1;
} else if (coordx(coord) > add(coordx($loc), sub($sx, 1))) {
    $dx = -1;
} else {
    $dx = 1;
}
return(~regicide_first_clear($loc, $dx, $dz, 1));

[proc,regicide_first_clear](coord $loc, int $dx, int $dz, int $n)(coord)
def_coord $c = movecoord($loc, multiply($dx, $n), 0, multiply($dz, $n));
if (map_blocked($c) = false) {
    return($c);
}
if ($n >= 10) {
    // Further than anything in Isafdar is thick. Put the player down rather than leave them
    // standing on the obstacle; no placement in the map reaches this.
    return($c);
}
return(~regicide_first_clear($loc, $dx, $dz, add($n, 1)));

[proc,regicide_trap_passed](int $at1, int $at99)(boolean)
def_int $chance = add($at1, divide(multiply(sub($at99, $at1), sub(stat(agility), 1)), 98));
if (random(1000) < $chance) {
    return(true);
}
return(false);

// ===== Leaf trap: regicide_pitfall_corner/mid/side, op1=Jump =====
[oploc1,regicide_pitfall_corner] @regicide_leaf_trap;
[oploc1,regicide_pitfall_mid] @regicide_leaf_trap;
[oploc1,regicide_pitfall_side] @regicide_leaf_trap;

[label,regicide_leaf_trap]
def_coord $end = ~regicide_obstacle_end(loc_coord, 1, 1, loc_angle);
mes("You try to jump over the pile of leaves...");
p_delay(0);
if (~regicide_trap_passed(707, 1000) = false) {
    // "You climb back out on the same side you fell from" - so no movement at all on a fail, which
    // is also what keeps a bad roll from dropping anybody into the pit tiles themselves.
    mes("...but you misjudge it and fall through onto the spikes!");
    sound_synth(human_hit2, 1, 0);
    ~damage_self(add(random(18), 1));
    return;
}
~forcemove($end);
mes("...and clear it easily.");

// ===== Tripwire: regicide_trap_tripwire, op1=Step-over =====
[oploc1,regicide_trap_tripwire]
def_coord $end = ~regicide_obstacle_end(loc_coord, 1, 2, loc_angle);
mes("You try to step over the tripwire...");
p_delay(0);
if (~regicide_trap_passed(121, 609) = false) {
    mes("...but you catch your foot, and four crossbows fire out of the twigs!");
    ~damage_self(10);
    queue(poison_player, 0, 2);
    return;
}
~forcemove($end);
mes("...and step over it safely.");

// ===== Stick trap: regicide_trap_woodspring, op1=Pass =====
[oploc1,regicide_trap_woodspring]
def_coord $end = ~regicide_obstacle_end(loc_coord, 3, 1, loc_angle);
mes("You try to pass the tied sticks...");
p_delay(0);
if (~regicide_trap_passed(121, 609) = false) {
    mes("...but you set the spring off and it knocks you back!");
    ~damage_self(8);
    return;
}
~forcemove($end);
mes("...and pass without incident.");

// ===== Log balances: regicide_logbalance1/2/3_start, op1=Cross =====
//
// THREE LOGS, ALL THREE DEAD. Nothing in the codebase named regicide_logbalance at all, so every
// one of them took the click and did nothing - and they are not scenery. Flood-filled on the
// ground plane, Isafdar is a handful of bands of open forest separated by solid scenery, and the
// dense-forest crossings above only join four of them. The logs join the rest: without them the
// band the Well of Voyage puts you out into reaches 494 tiles and stops, with Iorwerth Camp, the
// Poison Waste, the tracker and Tyras Camp all on the far side of a river nobody could cross.
//
// Each log is a row of regicide_logbalance1/2 ground decorations with a _start placement on each
// bank, and both banks carry the SAME _start type - so one trigger each, and the pair of bank
// coords tells the handler which way the player is going. The spans are not all the same length
// (the eastern one is five tiles between banks, the other two are four), which is why the shared
// ~log_balance_x/_z procs in skill_agility/scripts/log_balances.rs2 are not reused here: those
// derive both ends from a centre tile and assume a three-tile log.
//
// No Agility gate. The quest's own guide crosses these with nothing in the requirement list, and
// the 45-Agility figure the wiki gives belongs to the later logs over the river north of the
// forest, which are not these. No fail chance either, for the reason log_balances.rs2 gives for
// the two shortcut logs: a fall needs a specific in-river tile to wash the player up from and
// guessing one would be worse than leaving it out.

// Iorwerth Camp, west of the camp gate: banks at x=2197 and x=2201, z=3237.
[oploc1,regicide_logbalance1_start] ~regicide_log_cross_x(0_34_50_21_37, 0_34_50_25_37);
// Centre of the forest: banks at x=2259 and x=2263, z=3250.
[oploc1,regicide_logbalance2_start] ~regicide_log_cross_x(0_35_50_19_50, 0_35_50_23_50);
// East, on the way in from the Well of Voyage: banks at z=3233 and z=3238, x=2290.
[oploc1,regicide_logbalance3_start] ~regicide_log_cross_z(0_35_50_50_33, 0_35_50_50_38);

[proc,regicide_log_cross_x](coord $west, coord $east)
// Which bank the player is on, decided by the midpoint rather than by which loc was clicked -
// p_arrivedelay leaves them beside the start tile, not on it, and either bank's loc can be
// clicked from either side of the river.
if (coordx(coord) > divide(add(coordx($west), coordx($east)), 2)) {
    ~regicide_log_walk(~regicide_first_clear($west, -1, 0, 0));
    return;
}
~regicide_log_walk(~regicide_first_clear($east, 1, 0, 0));

[proc,regicide_log_cross_z](coord $south, coord $north)
if (coordz(coord) > divide(add(coordz($south), coordz($north)), 2)) {
    ~regicide_log_walk(~regicide_first_clear($south, 0, -1, 0));
    return;
}
~regicide_log_walk(~regicide_first_clear($north, 0, 1, 0));

// The far bank's own tile is where the player should end up, but on two of the three logs that
// tile carries the _start decoration on solid ground, so the walk goes on to the first tile past
// it. $n starts at 0 for that reason: the bank itself is the first candidate.
[proc,regicide_log_walk](coord $end)
mes("You step onto the log...");
sound_synth(log_balance, 2, 0);
~agility_force_move(0, human_walk_logbalance, $end);
mes("...and step off on the other side.");
